      "data": {
        "title": "STRIDE em uma tabela"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "1cbaec8c-e62f-4118-b725-ddf24e1dfaae",
          "type": "comparison_table",
          "position": 0,
          "data": {
            "columns": [
              "Letra",
              "Ameaça",
              "Propriedade quebrada",
              "Defesa típica"
            ],
            "rows": [
              [
                "S",
                "Spoofing — forjar identidade",
                "Authentication",
                "MFA, certificados, signed tokens"
              ],
              [
                "T",
                "Tampering — modificar dado",
                "Integrity",
                "HMAC, checksums, signatures, WORM"
              ],
              [
                "R",
                "Repudiation — negar ação",
                "Non-repudiation",
                "Logs imutáveis, audit trail, signatures"
              ],
              [
                "I",
                "Information disclosure",
                "Confidentiality",
                "Encryption at rest + in transit, least privilege"
              ],
              [
                "D",
                "Denial of service",
                "Availability",
                "Rate limiting, autoscaling, circuit breakers"
              ],
              [
                "E",
                "Elevation of privilege",
                "Authorization",
                "RBAC, input validation, no shared state"
              ]
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "904534af-4926-4dc0-a5b0-9abc82a4e40e",
      "type": "section",
      "position": 1,
      "data": {
        "title": "DFD — o mapa pra pensar ameaças"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "21553a95-973c-47dd-b288-f59492712d07",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "position": 0,
          "data": {
            "content": [
              {
                "text": " Data Flow Diagram é o template pra aplicar STRIDE. Desenhe "
              },
              {
                "text": "entidades",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "text": " (user, DB, serviço externo), "
              },
              {
                "text": "processos",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "text": ", "
              },
              {
                "text": "data stores",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "text": " e "
              },
              {
                "text": "trust boundaries",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "text": " (onde nível de confiança muda). "
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "8623fe3b-c807-402c-bd13-a55f47ab284f",
          "type": "code_block",
          "position": 1,
          "data": {
            "language": "text",
            "code": "[Browser]  ─HTTPS─▶  [API]  ─TLS─▶  [DB]\n           ▲                │\n           │                └─HMAC──▶ [Webhook Target]\n        trust boundary:\n        - User → API: spoofing (auth fraca?), tampering (TLS cert errado?)\n        - API → DB: info disclosure (cred hardcoded?), elevation (SQLi?)\n        - API → Webhook: tampering (replay sem HMAC?), repudiation (sem log?)"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "1a7f3d19-ec3b-4f06-aff3-2de19f3dc8b2",
          "type": "callout",
          "position": 2,
          "data": {
            "variant": "info",
            "title": "",
            "content": "Cada seta que cruza trust boundary é candidato a ameaça. Sente com o STRIDE ao lado e pergunte pra cada seta: que S/T/R/I/D/E pode acontecer aqui?"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "65dc2688-4e70-4286-9ae3-600868387012",
      "type": "section",
      "position": 2,
      "data": {
        "title": "DREAD → CVSS: priorizando"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "3f6fcb24-286a-447e-ad3b-9832ab7f73f3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "position": 0,
          "data": {
            "content": [
              {
                "text": " DREAD soma pontos em Damage/Reproducibility/Exploitability/Affected/Discoverability. Foi criticado por ser subjetivo. "
              },
              {
                "text": "CVSS 4.0",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "text": " (Common Vulnerability Scoring System) substituiu em 2026 pra priorização objetiva — vetor com attack surface, complexity, privileges required, user interaction, scope, CIA impact. "
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "f33b4a92-07a7-46bb-b567-458a9358998a",
          "type": "code_block",
          "position": 1,
          "data": {
            "language": "text",
            "code": "CVSS 4.0 Base Score exemplo:\nAV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:H/SI:H/SA:H\n= 10.0 (Critical) — atacante via rede, sem auth, impacto total"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "22e0b137-31e1-43c3-a464-13fe3a121b58",
      "type": "section",
      "position": 3,
      "data": {
        "title": "Operacionalizando: Threat Dragon ou markdown"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "e460bc70-d240-44ad-b755-5faa246e804c",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "position": 0,
          "data": {
            "content": [
              {
                "text": " Ferramentas: "
              },
              {
                "text": "OWASP Threat Dragon",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "text": " (open source, desenha DFD), "
              },
              {
                "text": "Microsoft Threat Modeling Tool",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "text": " (free, Windows), "
              },
              {
                "text": "PyTM",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "text": " (code-first em Python). Alternativa pragmática: markdown template no repo com DFD em mermaid + tabela STRIDE. Versiona junto com o código. "
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "edd9b374-2e23-49b6-b279-f31f4ac6b2d7",
          "type": "callout",
          "position": 1,
          "data": {
            "variant": "success",
            "title": "",
            "content": "Integre no PR template: \"Qual trust boundary este PR toca? Que STRIDE aplicamos?\". Faz threat modeling virar hábito, não evento."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}